From a06e8610b79ab670d642fde412a6df5b03146cd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 09:31:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/56] Lift unstable args in dependent methods with qualified
 types

When a method has qualified-type dependencies (in param types or result
type), unstable arguments cause SkolemType creation in safeSubstParam,
which leaks into qualified types. Override typedArg in ApplyToUntyped
to lift unstable args to val defs via a new LiftUnstable lifter. Thanks
to the preceding typeOfArg refactoring, the lifted type flows naturally
into safeSubstParam for substitution into remaining formals.

