Subject: [PATCH 34/56] Add transitivity reasoning for < in e-graph

Track strict upper/lower bounds per e-node. When `a < b` is merged
with true, propagate transitivity: if `b < c` or `d < a` are also
known, derive `a < c` or `d < b` respectively.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
