From e9f248202afe3bf506925d0b9a039f2eaf156b34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 16:34:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/56] Tighten qualified types argument lifting

Tighten the argument lifting logic for qualified types: instead of
lifting all unstable arguments when any qualifier exists, only lift
an argument if it is specifically referred to from a qualifier in
another parameter type or the result type (via TermParamRef), or if
its own type contains a qualifier (self-referencing case). Also only
lift when qualified types are enabled, and skip lifting inside
annotations (detected by walking parent contexts for Mode.InAnnotation).

Add a printing test qualified-types-lifting to verify the behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
