From 2e7c85b7225fa676ad885999c01d35db673f0697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 19:31:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/56] Break cyclic references for self-referencing qualified
 return types

When a method's return type is a qualified type whose qualifier
references the method itself (e.g., `def fib(n: Int): {res: Int with
res == fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)}`), computing the method's signature
would re-enter the completer, causing a CyclicReference error.

Fix this by pre-installing a provisional method type with just the
parent type (without the qualifier) before typing the full return type.
This follows the same pattern used by TypeDefCompleter for F-bounds
(Namer.scala line 1082).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
