Subject: [PATCH 45/56] Add if-then-else support in ENode/EGraph qualifier
 system

Add Op.IfThenElse as a new ternary operator in the ENode system,
allowing qualifiers to contain conditional expressions. This enables
writing qualified types like:

  def fib(n: Int): {res: Int with
    if n == 0 then res == 0
    else if n == 1 then res == 1
    else res == fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)
  }

The implementation covers:
- fromTree: converts tpd.If to OpApply(IfThenElse, ...)
- toTree: converts back to tpd.If
- normalizeOp: reduces when cond is true/false or branches are equal
- Pretty-printing in prettyString and toText

