From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 22:50:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/56] Add lambda beta reduction in EGraph

Implement beta reduction for Apply(Lambda, args) nodes in the EGraph,
enabling the qualifier solver to resolve predicates accessed through
constructor fields (e.g. box.p.apply(x) where p is a lambda).

Key changes:
- Add betaReduce method that substitutes ENodeParamRef in lambda body
- Add lambda.apply normalization in normalizeSelect
- Fix EGraph merge order: constructor-wrapping Apply/TypeApply and
  Lambda nodes now take priority over Select, so the repair chain
  correctly propagates field resolution and beta reduction
- Fix multi-arg beta reduction: reverse args to match de Bruijn order

