From 5b4a619629c155419a6b705e4f86ddea14d2e308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 23:28:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 51/56] Add return type assumptions for function applications

When the qualifier solver encounters a function call like f(x), it now
extracts the function's return type qualifier and substitutes method
params with actual args to produce an assumption. For example,
if f returns {res: Int with res == x + 1}, calling f(3) produces
the assumption f(3) == 3 + 1.

Also bumps EGraph repair iteration limit from 100 to 1000, as
recursive return type expansion can require more repair steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
