From ad6a1b4a3fca4929ccb4398fa5e3af3354a56edd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Mar 2026 01:05:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] Promote Any_== to OpApply(Equal) when receiver type is
 known

When qualifiers are written with type parameters (e.g., `g(f(a)) == a`
in a trait), `==` resolves to `Any_==` since the concrete type is
unknown. After type substitution instantiates the type parameter, a new
`promoteAnyEquals` pass converts these to `OpApply(Equal, ...)` when the
receiver type is a known value type or case class.

Also adds `mapChildren`/`map` helpers on ENode, extracts shared
`resolvedInfo` helper, and simplifies `resultTypeAssumptions`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../tools/dotc/qualified_types/ENode.scala    | 104 +++++++++++++-----
